# .codifide/sensitive-paths — the tripwires this repository sets for itself.
# Owned by the Human Steward. Changing this file is a governance change (R3).
#
# You never pick a "mode". Work starts light. When a change touches a path listed here,
# the CI check (check-review-level.sh) raises it to the highest review level (R3) and says
# what is owed before merge. The list is read from the base branch, so the change being
# judged cannot shorten it.
#
# One entry per line. A trailing "/" means the whole directory. Globs (*, ?) are allowed.
# Matching is case-insensitive. Lines starting with "#" are comments.
#
# List the places where a mistake hurts a person, loses money, or cannot be undone.
# Conventional auth, crypto, key, migration and infrastructure paths are already covered
# by the script; list what is specific to you. Examples (remove the "#" to use one):
#
# src/billing/rules/
# src/clinical/measures/
# services/patient-data/
# config/production*
